  "result": "The file is `src/lib/rate-limit.ts`. It holds both pieces:\n\n- **How many tries each action gets:** the `RATE_LIMIT_BUCKETS` table sets a limit for each kind of action. Password resets (`\"auth:password-reset\"`) start with 5 tries and earn back 1 per minute. Any action not in the table gets `DEFAULT_BUCKET`.\n- **The \"out of tries\" decision:** `consumeRateLimit` first adds back the tries earned since the last request. It then sets `allowed = tokens >= cost` and returns a `resetAt` time, which is the \"come back later\" moment.\n\n`src/actions/auth/reset-password.ts` only calls `consumeRateLimit`. When the answer is \"not allowed\", it throws a `RateLimitedError`. It doesn't make the decision or declare the limits itself.\n\nANSWER: src/lib/rate-limit.ts",
